mode: "100644"
text: "# The CLICK framework — design a thumbnail that earns the click honestly\n\nA thumbnail's whole job is the **click that leads to a watch** — so it has to be a **promise the video\nkeeps**, designed as a **unit with the title**, and **legible on a phone**. CLICK gets there. The agent\n**designs + briefs + plans the test**; a **human or image tool makes the raster**; the **YouTube thumbnail\nis uploaded + A/B-tested natively** (no WoopSocial field).\n\n## C — Clarify the promise\n- Write the **one-sentence promise** (\"this video shows [audience] how/why [outcome] by [mechanism]\").\n  Design the **thumbnail + title as one unit** — **show vs tell, never repeat.** **Promise, not poster** —\n  the watch-time A/B test punishes clickbait.\n\n## L — Lead with one focal point\n- **One or two hero elements**, one focal point; **minimal/blurred background.** Parseable in **under a\n  second.** A single **directional element** (arrow/gaze/circle) to point at the key detail.\n\n## I — Invoke genuine emotion\n- An **expressive, genuine face** with **gaze** pointing at the key element — **if it adds context.** Skip\n  the face when the brand is concept-focused or the visual subject is stronger. **Match the expression to\n  the content** (no fake shock).\n\n## C — Contrast + concise text\n- **High contrast:** complementary pairs, **avoid YouTube red/white**, **60-30-10**, pass the **B&W test**,\n  works in light + dark mode. **0–4 bold sans-serif words** with an outline, ~20–30% of frame, **not a\n  duplicate of the title.** **Mobile-legible at ~168×94**; **safe zones** (avoid bottom-right badge +\n  bottom 15%). **Specs: 1280×720, 16:9, JPG/PNG.**\n\n## K — Keep testing\n- **3 meaningfully-different concepts** (different promises/emotions), changing **ONE variable** so results\n  attribute. **Native Test & Compare** picks by **watch-time share** (not Shorts; needs traffic; ~14 days).\n  A **human uploads + runs** it in Studio. **Keep a testing log**; hold a **brand-consistent template.**\n\n## The thumbnail brief a request should fill\n```\nPROMISE: one sentence; thumbnail+title as a unit (show vs tell, no repeat); promise not poster\nFOCAL POINT: one hero element + minimal background; optional directional element\nFACE/EMOTION: genuine expression + gaze (or skip if no context)\nCONTRAST/TEXT: complementary high contrast (avoid YT red/white, 60-30-10, B&W test); 0-4 bold words + outline; safe zones; 1280x720\nTEST: 3 meaningfully-different concepts, one variable; native Test & Compare (watch-time share); human uploads/runs; raster by image tool/designer; CTR native (never fabricated)\n```\n"
